{{Quote|We will leave Orto Plutonia under the watchful eyes of the Talz, from this day forth. And recognize your sovereignty as a free and equal people.|Riyo Chuchi, to Thi-Sen|<ref name="Trespass" />}}
The '''Talz''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]]s [[Alzoc III]] and [[Orto Plutonia]], on which they remained undiscovered until the [[Clone Wars]]. Their discovery caused a [[One-Day War|brief war]] between a [[Talz village]] and the [[Pantoran Assembly]] due to [[Chairman]] [[Chi Cho]] of [[Pantora]] believing they were a hostile force. After the [[death]] of Cho, Pantoran [[Senator]] [[Riyo Chuchi]] talked and ended the war with the [[Chief]]tain of the village, [[Thi-Sen]], after which the Talz were officially recognized as a free and equal people and were allowed to live peacefully on their [[homeworld]].

==Biology and appearance==
{{Quote|Technically, Muftak, I believe your kind may ''be'' animals.|Djas Puhr|<ref name="The Kloo Horn Cantina Caper">{{StoryCite|story=The Kloo Horn Cantina Caper|book=From a Certain Point of View}}</ref>}}
[[File:Talz-SoTR.png|250px|left|thumb|Talz imprisoned as slaves during the Clone Wars.]]
Talz were large bipeds covered in thick, shaggy [[Color|white]] [[Hair|fur]] with sharp [[Claw|talons]] capping their five-fingered hands. They possessed four black [[eye]]s &mdash; the small eyes used for day vision and the larger eyes for night vision &mdash; and a small [[Mouth|proboscis]] for [[Diet|feeding]] and communicating.<ref name="CEUE">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> The shaggy fur coat protected them against the [[Temperature|freezing]] conditions of their [[Water|ice]] and snow habitat.<ref name="VE" />

==Society and culture==
{{Quote|Steady Anakin, they're only curious. Let's not provoke them as the droids and our troops must have done.|Obi-Wan Kenobi|<ref name="Trespass" />}}
The Talz were a primitive civilization that used few tools<ref name="CEUE" /> and lived a simple life in a harsh environment.<ref name="DB Talz" /> They organized themselves in tribes led by [[chief]]tains,<ref name="Trespass" /> and used the native [[narglatch]]es as mounts and protection.<ref name="DB Talz" /> They had a [[language]] of their own, called [[Talzzi]],<ref name="The Complete Season One" /> but were unable to speak [[Galactic Basic Standard]].<ref name="Trespass" />

==History==
{{Quote|They only want to be left alone. The droids attacked them, and I'm afraid our outpost got caught in the middle.|Obi-Wan Kenobi|<ref name="Trespass" />}}
[[File:Ramakak.png|250px|thumb|right|Ramakak, a Talz]]
The Talz hailed from [[Alzoc III]]<ref name="Helmet 2" /> and [[Orto Plutonia]], a frigid [[planet]] located in the [[Pantora system]].<ref name="DB Orto">{{Databank|orto-plutonia|Orto Plutonia}}</ref> During the [[Clone Wars]], both the [[Galactic Republic]] and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] attempted to establish outposts on Orto Plutonia, only to be wiped out by the natives.<ref name="DB Talz" /> After the attack on the Republic base, [[Jedi General]]s [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Anakin Skywalker]] arrived with a detachment of [[clone trooper]]s, which included Skywalker's [[Clone Captain]], [[Rex]]. The Jedi and clones were also joined by the [[droid]]s [[C-3PO]] and [[R2-D2]], and representatives of the planet [[Pantora]], which was in the same [[Star system|system]]. These representatives were [[Chairman]] [[Chi Cho]], [[Senator]] [[Riyo Chuchi]]. Cho believed that whoever had attacked the Republic were an aggressive force, and waged war on the Talz who had attacked: Chieftain [[Thi-Sen]] and his [[Talz village|Talz tribe]]. The ensuing battle caused heavy casualties on both sides, including the two [[Pantoran guard]]s who tried to protect the chairman, and the majority of the [[clone cold assault trooper]]s minus Rex [[Gender|himself]] and a few other [[Cloning|clones]]. The two Pantoran guards were also [[Death|killed]], and Cho was badly injured. He ordered Chuchi to destroy the Talz, but she refused, as his actions had been seen as being out of order by the [[Pantoran Assembly]]. After hearing this Cho was left in disbelief and with his last breaths said that he had died for his people, and then died from his injuries. Chuchi approached Thi-sen, and brought C-3PO as a translator. Chuchi explained that to die for ones people was a great sacrifice, but to live for them was a greater sacrifice. She said she would live for her people, and Thi-sen said he would do the same. The two groups departed as equals, and the Talz were recognized as the sovereign and free people of Orto Plutonia.<ref name="Trespass" />

During the [[Imperial Era]], the Talz were still a primitive species. They used few tools, and they were only taken to space by [[enslaver]]s.<ref name="CVD">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref> Nevertheless, the Talz [[Insurgency on Orto Plutonia|fought an insurgency]] against the [[Galactic Empire]] on Orto Plutonia.<ref name="Forged">''[[Forged in Battle]]''</ref>

==Talz in the galaxy==
[[File:Muftak-ANH.png|220px|left|thumb|[[Muftak]], a Talz who resided in [[Mos Eisley]] on [[Tatooine]].]]
By the time of the Clone Wars, the Talz were not advanced enough to master [[Realspace|space]] travel.<ref name="Trespass" /> At least three Talz were [[Slavery|slaves]] that were held in the [[Zygerrian slave market|slave market]] on [[Zygerria]].<ref name="Slaves of the Republic">{{TCW|Slaves of the Republic}}</ref> At some point during the [[Imperial Era]], the elderly Talz [[Broo]] lived in the [[Imperial Elderblock 26-0640]] on the Empire's [[capital]] [[Coruscant]].<ref name="Elderblock">{{InsiderCite|236|Galactic Tales: A Death in Elderblock 26-0640}}</ref> By the time of the Galactic Civil War, the species was still primitive, and Talz were taken out to space by slavers.<ref name="CVD" /> During the war, some Talz could be found on planets such as [[Tatooine]],<ref name="Episode IV" /> [[Espirion]],<ref name="Princess Leia, Part V">[[Princess Leia 5|''Princess Leia'' 5]]</ref> and [[Son-tuul]].<ref name="Darth Vader 7">[[Darth Vader (2015) 7|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 7]]</ref> At least [[Muftak|one]] Talz, [[Muftak]], was present at [[Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina]] when Obi-Wan Kenobi saved [[Luke Skywalker]] from [[Cornelius Evazan]] and [[Ponda Baba]] by [[Dismemberment|cutting]] off the latter's arm.<ref name="Episode IV" />

By the waning years of the [[Galactic Civil War]], some Imperial personnel considered Talz meat delicious.<ref name="Life Debt">''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]''</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The Talz species originally appeared in the Mos Eisley Cantina in [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|Star Wars Episode IV ''A New Hope'']]. Their culture elaborated in the TV series [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'']], in the fifteenth episode in [[The Clone Wars: Season One|Season One]] titled ''[[Trespass]].''<ref name="Trespass" /> [[George Lucas]] wanted to do a classic Western story in which seemingly primitive native people fought back against a superior military in order to defend their homeland. While designing the clothing and habitat of the Talz, the creators drew upon [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inuit Inuit], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigenous_peoples_of_the_Americas indigenous North American] and prehistoric cultures.<ref name="The Art of Star Wars: The Clone Wars">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''</ref>

